#!/usr/bin/env python3
# ==============================================================================
# NAME     : dev/planning-cycle-acceptance
# PURPOSE  : Bounded acceptance of a planning cycle and its finalisation (v10 C7
#            with B11) on two frames that share a PowerHA cluster: the frame of
#            the standby node and the frame of its primary.
#
#            The two frames are named by their pseudonyms (sys_...). Their staged
#            captures are cloned into a disposable work tree (copy-on-write where
#            the file system offers it), with this repository's nfit, nfit-profile
#            and etc/. The captures themselves are not written to.
#
#            On the work tree it
#              1. analyses both frames into one planning cycle (one model);
#              2. finalises the cycle, and finalises it once more;
#              3. with --both-orders, repeats 1 and 2 in the opposite order in a
#                 second cycle;
#            and reports
#              - each analysis and finalisation: exit status and elapsed time;
#              - each PowerHA standby whose primary is on the other frame: its
#                provisional and final entitlement / VPs, whether it was set or
#                left unresolved (with the reason), and its final action;
#              - whether the CSV row and the saved plan agree;
#              - whether the second finalisation changed any output;
#              - with --both-orders, whether both orders give the same final row;
#              - from the saved plans: which partner supplied each floor and from
#                which target, how each frame read the roles, the role evidence
#                window and the latest role period against the period the
#                primary was sized on, and any handover hold;
#              - whether CSV, saved plan and the rationale's finalisation block
#                agree on the pool totals, pool alerts and pool prerequisites;
#              - the cycle status, the cycle's size on disk and the allocation
#                footprint.
#            --read WORK gives the last two from a kept work tree (--keep),
#            without running anything.
#            The report passes through dev/nfit-redact: LPARs and frames appear
#            by pseudonym only. Nothing is printed if the filter cannot run.
#
#            Needs in etc/nfit.vms.cfg: ha_peer for the cluster, and
#            ha_sizing = standby_share. Without them no standby is sized from
#            its primary and there is nothing to finalise; the tool stops before
#            the analyses unless --force.
#
#            --standby-fixed sys_PSEUDONYM=ENT gives one of the two frames a
#            fixed standby entitlement for this run: a [MGSYS:<frame>] stanza
#            (ha_sizing = standby_fixed, standby_entitlement = ENT) is added to
#            the work tree's copy of nfit.vms.cfg only. The tool resolves the
#            frame's name itself; etc/nfit.vms.cfg is not changed. Each standby
#            on that frame is then checked: it takes the fixed figure on the
#            VPs its own workload needs, or the figure is not applied and the
#            node keeps its ordinary recommendation, with the cause stated; it
#            is final at analysis, is not touched by finalisation, and both
#            orders agree. The report prints what each decision rested on (VP
#            requirements, reduction-safety verdict, sustained workload). An
#            LPAR whose own stanza sets ha_sizing keeps its own policy; the
#            report says which source each standby's policy came from.
# USAGE    : dev/planning-cycle-acceptance sys_FIRST sys_SECOND
#                --captures DIR | --stage DIR ... [--model MODEL]
#            (NFIT_CAPTURES may hold the capture root; no location is built in)
#                [--enddate YYYY-MM-DD] [--config FILE] [--both-orders]
#                [--standby-fixed sys_PSEUDONYM=ENT]
#                [--work DIR] [--keep] [--force]
#            dev/planning-cycle-acceptance --read WORK
# ==============================================================================
